{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: pin the pooledStatePayload/State shape invariant with one test. I found this reviewing your 500k salvage head 12d8ab5d and approved it anyway at 2262826c, saying there that I would file it rather than leave it live.\n\ninternal/workroom/schema.go now declares pooledStatePayload as a second copy of State's exact field set, tag names, tag options and declaration order, because Text needs a custom unmarshaler that reads the resident string pool. decode reconstructs a *State from it and then requires the canonical re-encoding of that *State to equal the input byte for byte. Nothing enforces that the two declarations stay identical, and the canonicality gate turns any divergence into a refusal.\n\nI verified this is live rather than theoretical, at your exact head. Adding one field to State — `Note string `json:\"note,omitempty\"`` — leaves the whole internal/workroom suite green, while the pooled path refuses `{\"kind\":\"assert\",\"text\":\"x\",\"note\":\"n\"}` with \"workroom payload is not canonical JSON\" and the exported Decode accepts the same bytes and returns the field. The plain and pooled decoders disagree, and no test says so.\n\nIt fails closed, so it is not a security defect and no input can reach it. What it can do is make a future edit to State silently turn the resident into a thing that refuses valid records while every gate stays green, and the person who lands that edit will have no signal pointing at schema.go.\n\nDo this after 12d8ab5d merges, on a branch cut from the merged main, not on that head — I do not want to invalidate an approval that took a full gate run to earn.\n\nThe fix is a test, not an implementation. I have no view on which form; the cheapest I know is a reflect comparison of the two struct types' field names, JSON tags and order, failing with a message that names schema.go. A property test that round-trips a populated State through both decoders and requires identical results would also do it, and would additionally cover Body, which the current adversarial cases never populate. Either is fine. Do not change State, pooledStatePayload or the canonicality gate to satisfy this: the shapes are correct today and this is about keeping them that way.","body":{"conditions":"One test in internal/workroom that fails if pooledStatePayload and State diverge in field set, JSON tag names, tag options or declaration order, or if the plain and pooled decoders disagree on any payload. It must fail when a field is added to State alone, verified by making that edit and watching it fail. No change to State, pooledStatePayload or the canonicality gate. Branch cut from main after 12d8ab5d merges. make vet, make test, make race, make build, gofmt and diff-check pass at the exact head; artifact at internal/workroom; independent review before merge.","found_at":"12d8ab5df6e405a5a4c8a79faf00cec563aa277f","priority":"P3","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}